                                    </div>

                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>Is Pinterest actually worth investing in for home decor?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes — for home decor specifically. Pinterest still drives 2-4x more efficient top-funnel spend than Meta for this category. Requires content-heavy operation (10-20 pins per week per collection).</p>
                                        <h3>How much does AR room preview cost to add?</h3>
                                        <p>$18K-50K one-time via Poplar Studio, Ochre Bio, or custom WebAR. ROI typically pays back in 6-12 months via CVR lift on high-value SKUs.</p>
                                        <h3>Should home decor brands use Amazon?</h3>
                                        <p>Selectively. Amazon works for high-turnover accessible SKUs but cannibalises brand storytelling. Most successful D2C decor brands sell on Amazon only for hero SKUs and reserve premium collections for brand.com.</p>
                                        <h3>What is the biggest home decor D2C failure mode?</h3>
                                        <p>Under-investing in photography. Home decor sells on lifestyle imagery. Product-only shots on white background lose to competitors with in-context styling every time.</p>
